  "copy": {
    "fr": {
      "tagline": "Un casse-briques aux billes comptées. Vise, puis touche l'écran pour allumer les boutons et enfermer la bille entre les briques de couleur.",
      "tags": [
        "Tap pour piéger",
        "Casse-briques",
        "Interrupteurs"
      ]
    },
    "en": {
      "tagline": "A brick breaker with a limited supply of balls. Aim, then tap to switch the buttons on and trap the ball with the coloured bricks.",
      "tags": [
        "Tap to trap",
        "Breakout",
        "Switch buttons"
      ]
    }
  },
  "description": "Coloured glass and banks of switches over a lake of lava. The ball breaks every pane of glass and flies straight past the dark buttons — until you tap: then they light up and turn solid, and the ball bounces off them and can never break them. Tap while the ball is inside a pocket of glass and it is shut in with it, runs faster and eats the whole room; tap again to let it out, or the game opens an empty pocket for you. Thirty boards across five biomes, each with its own bonus bricks: row and column blasts, bombs and multiball, the big ball, the fireball that burns through the glass and the magnet that pulls it in — and each biome brings its own living glass too: warp panes that jump every three seconds, split panes that burst into new glass, a seed that grows glass around it and electric panes behind a shield that comes and goes. Each biome teaches it in six stages — one colour, then all five and what each pays, its power, its living glass, the mix and a finale — and the stars are the wall's, not the score's: half of it, four fifths, and three for a clear or for four fifths within the level's par of balls. The dotted sight solves five bounces ahead.",
